messages:
anna_sales: Peter's POC hit a streaming failure in their Android embedded webview during today's demo. They get JSON.parse errors and the stream drops after ~40s. Demo interrupted.
dave_se: Can you paste the client console and a snippet from the network capture? Is desktop affected or only the embedded webview?
peter_customer: Only the mobile webview. Desktop Chrome works fine. Client error: "Uncaught SyntaxError: Unexpected end of JSON input at parseStream (app.js:512)". Network shows SSE data lines that look truncated. Copying a short sequence from the capture: \nevent: message\ndata: {"idx":101,"text":"Hello"}\n\nevent: message\ndata: {"idx":102,"text":"This is a very lo\n\n"

The second data payload is cut mid-object and the webview tries to JSON.parse it.

olga_oncall: Infra: I see a cluster of 429 spikes and a couple of upstream resets in the edge logs for that org at the same time. LB shows "recv() failed (104: Connection reset by peer)" and proxy: "upstream timed out (110)". Could be proxy buffering + retry storm leading to partial frames.
dave_se: Two contributors likely: (1) client-side code assumes each SSE data: block is a complete JSON object, (2) network/proxy fragmentation or premature connection close truncates blocks. Recommend short-term mitigation: buffer incoming data lines client-side and only JSON.parse when buffer yields a valid object; increase keepalive and disable proxy buffering for streams.
ci-bot: canary v2.20.3 deployed eu-west-1 at 2110001000
anna_sales: Can we do a quick infra tweak + provide a tiny shim so they can avoid rebuilding the wrapper?
olga_oncall: I'll temporarily lower gateway retry aggression for that org and disable proxy_buffering on SSE routes in canary. I'll also add heartbeat comment lines (":\n") every 12s to keep connections alive.
peter_customer: That would help. We'd prefer a zero-build shim we can inject into the webview if possible.
dave_se: Share this minimal accumulator you can paste into the webview's JS runtime without rebuild: ```js
// SSE accumulator - handles split JSON across multiple data: events
let _acc = '';// accumulated text
function onSseData(dataLine) {
  // dataLine is the string from the event data: payload
  _acc += dataLine;
  try {
    const msg = JSON.parse(_acc);
    handleMessage(msg);
    _acc = '';
  } catch (err) {
    // incomplete JSON - wait for next chunk
    if (_acc.length > 128 * 1024) { _acc = ''; console.warn('dropping oversized partial'); }
  }
}
// optional: flush buffer after timeout if no progress
setInterval(() => { if (_acc && Date.now() - lastProgress > 5000) { _acc = ''; } }, 5000);
```
(Add a small guard to avoid stuck state.)
anna_sales: Peter, want us to apply the infra changes now and send the snippet?
peter_customer: Yes please 94 apply the canary infra changes and send the shim. We'll inject the JS and test in ~30m.
olga_oncall: Actions: (1) apply gateway retry throttle for org (done) (2) disable proxy buffering for SSE routes on canary (done) (3) enable 12s heartbeats on canary (in progress) (4) add partial-parse metric (queued). I'll post updates in #eng-runtime if the heartbeat rollout changes.
dave_se: For long-term, we'll add a note in the SDK guidance: SSE consumers must handle multi-chunk JSON payloads and not assume per-data JSON completeness. We'll add a small helper in the JS SDK.
anna_sales: Thanks everyone. Marking this POC as high-touch until the exec demo tomorrow. Peter will report back with results or new logs. :thumbsup:
peter_customer: Thanks team 94 testing now, will update in ~25m.
